---
---
<div class="hajnal-container">
    <div class="hajnal-header">
        <h3>The Hajnal Line & Prussia</h3>
        <p>John Hajnal’s (1965) famous demarcation between the Western European Marriage Pattern (late marriage, high celibacy) and the Eastern pattern.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="hajnal-visual">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 800 400" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet">
            <!-- Background Europe (Stylized) -->
            <rect x="0" y="0" width="800" height="400" fill="rgba(255,255,255,0.02)" rx="8" />
            
            <!-- Countries / Regions -->
            <path d="M 100 100 L 300 80 L 350 150 L 200 200 Z" fill="#2c3e50" opacity="0.5" /> <!-- Western Europe -->
            <path d="M 400 50 L 700 80 L 750 300 L 450 350 Z" fill="#2c3e50" opacity="0.3" /> <!-- Eastern Europe -->
            
            <!-- Prussia Overlay -->
            <path d="M 300 80 L 550 100 L 600 250 L 350 200 Z" fill="var(--accent)" opacity="0.6" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="2" />
            
            <!-- The Hajnal Line -->
            <line x1="450" y1="20" x2="350" y2="380" stroke="#c0392b" stroke-width="4" stroke-dasharray="10,10" id="hajnal-line" />
            
            <!-- Labels -->
            <text x="150" y="250" fill="white" font-size="14" font-weight="bold">WESTERN PATTERN</text>
            <text x="550" y="320" fill="white" font-size="14" font-weight="bold">EASTERN PATTERN</text>
            <text x="450" y="50" fill="var(--accent)" font-size="12" font-weight="bold">PRUSSIA (STRADDLING)</text>
            <text x="430" y="15" fill="#c0392b" font-size="10" transform="rotate(75, 430, 15)">ST. PETERSBURG</text>
            <text x="340" y="395" fill="#c0392b" font-size="10" transform="rotate(75, 340, 395)">TRIESTE</text>
        </svg>
    </div>

    <div class="hajnal-content">
        <div class="h-card">
            <h4>Western Side</h4>
            <p>Late marriage, nuclear households, and "Malthusian" preventive checks. Most of the Prussian Rhineland falls here.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="h-card highlight">
            <h4>The Prussia Paradox</h4>
            <p>Prussia was institutionalized as a Western state but geographically extended deep into the Eastern pattern. The Kulturkampf acted as a "Westernizing" shock to Eastern marital norms.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="h-card">
            <h4>Eastern Side</h4>
            <p>Early/universal marriage, joint households. The Polish provinces of Posen and East Prussia align with this pattern.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<style>
    .hajnal-container {
        margin: 6rem 0;
        background: var(--surface);
        border: 1px solid var(--border);
        padding: 3rem;
        border-radius: 8px;
    }

    .hajnal-header {
        margin-bottom: 3rem;
        text-align: center;
    }

    .hajnal-header h3 {
        font-size: 2rem;
        margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    }

    .hajnal-header p {
        opacity: 0.7;
        max-width: 600px;
        margin: 0 auto;
    }

    .hajnal-visual {
        margin-bottom: 3rem;
        filter: drop-shadow(0 0 20px rgba(0,0,0,0.5));
    }

    svg {
        width: 100%;
        height: auto;
    }

    #hajnal-line {
        filter: drop-shadow(0 0 5px #c0392b);
    }

    .hajnal-content {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(200px, 1fr));
        gap: 2rem;
    }

    .h-card {
        padding: 1.5rem;
        background: rgba(255,255,255,0.02);
        border: 1px solid var(--border);
        border-radius: 4px;
    }

    .h-card h4 {
        color: var(--accent);
        margin-bottom: 0.8rem;
        font-size: 1.1rem;
    }

    .h-card p {
        font-size: 0.85rem;
        line-height: 1.6;
        opacity: 0.7;
        margin: 0;
    }

    .h-card.highlight {
        border-color: var(--accent);
        background: rgba(212, 175, 55, 0.05);
    }
</style>
